From 0cd50dae7c40e1f821cbd96ddc77348403939326 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:16:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] jay: optionally do half float compute math in 32 bits

INTEL_PROMOTE_F16=1 (off by default) widens 16-bit float ALU ops of
compute shaders without cooperative matrices to 32 bits and folds the
f2f32(f2f16(x)) round trips. Not exact, but it removes the copies
between dword-strided halves (what float->half conversions and unpacked
halves give) and the packed halves 3-source half instructions need:
FSR4's preprocessing goes from 1891 to 1134 instructions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
